*==============================================================================
* OPAMP_FULL  -  behavioural op-amp macromodel (ngspice)
*
* Copyright (c) 2026 Stanislav Maslovski
* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause  (see LICENSE)
* Version 1.1 (2026-11). Developed with the help of Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).
*
* Pins: inp inn vcc vee out
*
* LINEAR EFFECTS
*   - finite DC gain A0, dominant pole, GBW, two extra poles (FP2, FP3)
*   - differential / common-mode input R and C (noiseless)
*   - CMRR and PSRR(+/-) with frequency roll-off (a zero in the coupling gain)
*   - output resistance (ROUT) and output capacitance
*   - input voltage noise (white + 1/f) and input current noise (white + 1/f,
*     FCIN = current-noise 1/f corner, independent on each input; 0 = off)
* NONLINEAR EFFECTS
*   - input offset voltage, input bias and offset currents
*   - input stage tanh() characteristic  -> slew rate and large-signal THD
*   - input common-mode range (gm collapses near the rails)
*   - optional differential input clamp (VCLMP, RCLMP)
*   - output voltage swing limited by the supplies (VHD/VLD headroom)
*   - output current limit (ISRC/ISNK), class-AB crossover dead-zone (VXO)
*   - supply current = quiescent + load current drawn from the right rail
*
* Defaults approximate a general-purpose 1 MHz bipolar op amp on +/-15 V
* (uA741-like typicals). Rail-to-rail example parameters are given at the end.
*
* Units: SR in V/s (0.5Meg = 0.5 V/us). PSRR/CMRR as ratios (31.6k = 90 dB).
*
* Notes
*   - VOS, the input voltage noise and the CMRR/PSRR error terms form one
*     error voltage in series with the + input, ahead of RID (RID is driven
*     by the internal V(vd)). So no spurious (VOS+en)/RID current flows in
*     the source resistance.
*   - All model-internal resistors are noiseless (VCCS form). The only noise
*     generators are Rnv, Rnp, Rnn (white), Dfa (1/f voltage) and Dfp1, Dfn1
*     (1/f current, FCIN > 0). Noise levels are
*     exact at TEMP = 27 C and scale like kT elsewhere.
*   - Bias currents: IB > 0 flows INTO the pins (NPN input); use IB < 0 for PNP.
*   - RIC || CIC is the common-mode input impedance with both inputs tied
*     together (datasheet convention): each pin gets 2*RIC || CIC/2.
*   - VCMN: the input common-mode voltage at which VOS is specified. The CMRR
*     error term is (Vcm - VCMN)/CMRR. The default is mid-supply.
*   - Differential clamp: anti-parallel diodes with drop VCLMP at 1 mA and
*     series resistance RCLMP. The default VCLMP=100 disables it (the 741 has
*     no clamp diodes; leakage < 1e-14 A at 15 V). For an OP27-style clamp use
*     VCLMP=0.7 RCLMP=100 (the original model's DIN diodes).
*   - Crossover: for |Iout| << VXO/ROUT the small-signal output resistance is
*     2*ROUT. It is ROUT once |Iout| > ~2*VXO/ROUT (2 mV/75 ohm ~ 50 uA).
*     Set VXO=0 for a plain ROUT everywhere.
*==============================================================================

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* ZCPL : out = K * (1 + s/(2*pi*FZ)) * in      (ideal zero, exact derivative)
* Used for CMRR(f) and PSRR(f): coupling into the input rises above FZ,
* i.e. the rejection ratio falls at 20 dB/dec. FHI limits the derivative.
* The derivative resistor is a noiseless VCCS.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt ZCPL in out PARAMS: K=1u FZ=1k FHI=20Meg
.param TAUZ={1/(6.283185307*FZ)} CD=1n
Ek  na 0 in 0 {K}
Cd  in nx {CD}
Gd  nx nv nx nv {6.283185307*FHI*CD}
Vs  nv 0 0
Hd  out na Vs {K*TAUZ/CD}
.ends ZCPL

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt OPAMP_FULL inp inn vcc vee out
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=200k GBW=1Meg SR=0.5Meg FP2=3Meg FP3=10Meg
+ VOS=1m IB=80n IOS=20n
+ RID=2Meg CID=1.4p RIC=200Meg CIC=1.5p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=200 PSRRP=31.6k PSRRN=31.6k FPSRR=100 VCCN=15 VEEN=-15
+ VCMN={0.5*(VCCN+VEEN)}
+ ENOISE=20n FCEN=200 INOISE=0.5p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=1.7m VHD=2 VLD=2 ICMHI=2 ICMLO=2 VK=0.15
+ ROUT=75 ISRC=25m ISNK=25m VXO=2m COUT=3p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100

* ---- derived constants -------------------------------------------------------
.param PI2=6.283185307
.param C1V=30p
.param IMAXV={SR*C1V}              ; input-stage tail current -> slew rate
.param GM0={PI2*GBW*C1V}           ; small-signal transconductance -> GBW
.param R1V={A0/GM0}                ; DC gain A0 = GM0*R1V
.param VNTH={sqrt(4*1.380649e-23*300.15*1e3)}   ; thermal noise of 1k at 27C
* 1/f source: diode biased at IFL. Its flicker voltage density is
* KF*IFL*(Vt/IFL)^2/f = KF*Vt^2/(IFL*f), so KF = ENOISE^2*FCEN*IFL/Vt^2.
* The two diodes also add white shot noise 2*(2*q*Vt^2/IFL), i.e.
* (0.21 nV/rtHz)^2 at 10 mA. It is subtracted from the white generator so
* that the total white density is exactly ENOISE (for ENOISE > 0.21 nV).
* (IFL much above 0.1 A upsets the transient time-step control.)
.param IFL=10m
.param VTN={1.380649e-23*300.15/1.602176634e-19}
.param KFV={ENOISE*ENOISE*FCEN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param ESH2={4*1.602176634e-19*VTN*VTN/IFL}
.param GENV={sqrt(max(ENOISE*ENOISE-ESH2,0))/VNTH}
.param GNI={INOISE/VNTH}
* 1/f current noise (FCIN > 0): one more flicker diode pair per input, so the
* two pins get independent noise. The flicker voltage of the pair is scaled to
* VNI*sqrt(FCIN/f) with VNI = 1 uV/rtHz and converted to current by GFI =
* INOISE/VNI, giving INOISE^2*FCIN/f. The pair's shot noise then adds only
* (0.21n/1u)^2 = 4e-8 of INOISE^2. FCIN = 0 disables the sources (GFI = 0).
.param KFI={1e-12*FCIN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param GFI={FCIN>0 ? INOISE/1u : 0}

* ---- input network (noiseless) -------------------------------------------------
* RID carries V(vd)/RID, i.e. it sits behind the series error voltage
* (VOS, noise, CMRR/PSRR), as if that voltage were in series with the + pin
Gid  inp inn vd 0 {1/RID}
Cid  inp inn {CID}
Gic1 inp 0 inp 0 {1/(2*RIC)}
Gic2 inn 0 inn 0 {1/(2*RIC)}
Cic1 inp 0 {CIC/2}
Cic2 inn 0 {CIC/2}
* bias currents flow INTO the pins for IB > 0 (NPN input)
Ibp  inp 0 DC {IB+IOS/2}
Ibn  inn 0 DC {IB-IOS/2}
* optional differential input clamp diodes: VCLMP = diode drop at 1 mA
* (set via the emission coefficient), RCLMP = series resistance
Dp1  inp inn DIN
Dp2  inn inp DIN
.model DIN D(IS=1e-15 N={VCLMP/(VTN*log(1e-3/1e-15))} RS={RCLMP})

* ---- noise sources (visible to .noise analysis only) ------------------------
* white voltage noise: thermal noise of a 1k resistor scaled by GENV
Rnv  nnv 0 1e3
* white current noise on each input
Rnp  nnp 0 1e3
Rnn  nnn 0 1e3
Gnp  0 inp nnp 0 {GNI}
Gnn  0 inn nnn 0 {GNI}
* 1/f voltage noise: flicker noise of a diode biased at IFL, minus an
* identical KF=0 diode so that the DC drop cancels
Ifa  0 nfa DC {IFL}
Dfa  nfa 0 DFLK
Ifb  0 nfb DC {IFL}
Dfb  nfb 0 DQ
Efl  nfl 0 nfa nfb 1
.model DFLK D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFV} AF=1)
.model DQ   D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* 1/f current noise, independent on each input (FCIN > 0)
Ifp1 0 nfp1 DC {IFL}
Dfp1 nfp1 0 DFLKI
Ifp2 0 nfp2 DC {IFL}
Dfp2 nfp2 0 DQ
Gfp  0 inp nfp1 nfp2 {GFI}
Ifn1 0 nfn1 DC {IFL}
Dfn1 nfn1 0 DFLKI
Ifn2 0 nfn2 DC {IFL}
Dfn2 nfn2 0 DQ
Gfn  0 inn nfn1 nfn2 {GFI}
.model DFLKI D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFI} AF=1)

* ---- CMRR and PSRR coupling into the input -----------------------------------
Bcm  ncm0 0 V = 0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-{VCMN}
Xcm  ncm0 ncm ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/CMRR} FZ={FCMRR}
Bps1 nps1i 0 V = V(vcc)-{VCCN}
Xps1 nps1i nps1 ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRP} FZ={FPSRR}
Bps2 nps2i 0 V = V(vee)-{VEEN}
Xps2 nps2i nps2 ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRN} FZ={FPSRR}

* ---- effective differential input voltage ------------------------------------
* = V(inp) - V(inn) + series error voltage (VOS + CMRR/PSRR terms + noise)
Bvd  vd 0 V = V(inp)-V(inn)+{VOS}+V(ncm)+V(nps1)+V(nps2)+{GENV}*V(nnv)+V(nfl)

* ---- input common-mode range window (0..1, 0.5 at the ICMR edge) ---------------
Bwin nwin 0 V = max(0.25*(1+tanh((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-V(vee)-{ICMLO})/{VK}))*(1+tanh((V(vcc)-{ICMHI}-0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))/{VK})),1e-3)

* ---- input stage + dominant pole (tanh gives slew limiting) ------------------
Bgm  0 n1 I = {IMAXV}*V(nwin)*tanh({GM0}*V(vd)/{IMAXV})
G1   n1 0 n1 0 {1/R1V}
C1   n1 0 {C1V}
* soft clamp of the gain node to the swing limits (fast overdrive recovery)
Bhi  nhi 0 V = V(vcc)-{VHD}
Blo  nlo 0 V = V(vee)+{VLD}
Bclp n1 0 I = {IMAXV/1e-3}*(max(V(n1)-V(nhi),0)+min(V(n1)-V(nlo),0))

* ---- higher-order poles (noiseless 1k / C sections) --------------------------
G2   0 n2 n1 0 1m
G2r  n2 0 n2 0 1m
C2   n2 0 {1/(PI2*FP2*1e3)}
G3   0 n3 n2 0 1m
G3r  n3 0 n3 0 1m
C3   n3 0 {1/(PI2*FP3*1e3)}

* ---- output stage ----------------------------------------------------------------
* Norton output: I = (V(n3)-V(out) with crossover dead-zone)/ROUT, hard-limited
Bicmd nicmd 0 V = min({ISRC},max(-{ISNK},((V(n3)-V(out))-0.5*{VXO}*tanh((V(n3)-V(out))/({VXO}+1e-9)))/{ROUT}))
* smooth split into source (from VCC) and sink (to VEE) currents:
* Bsrc - Bsnk = Icmd exactly, and the slope is well-defined at I = 0
Bsrc vcc out I = 0.5*(V(nicmd)+sqrt(V(nicmd)*V(nicmd)+1e-12))
Bsnk out vee I = 0.5*(sqrt(V(nicmd)*V(nicmd)+1e-12)-V(nicmd))
Iq   vcc vee DC {ICCQ}
Cout out 0 {COUT}
.ends OPAMP_FULL

*==============================================================================
* Example parameter sets (use with  X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_FULL PARAMS: ...)
*
* Generic CMOS rail-to-rail, 5 V single supply, 5 MHz, 5 V/us:
*   A0=100k GBW=5Meg SR=5Meg FP2=15Meg FP3=50Meg VOS=2m IB=1p IOS=0.5p
*   RID=1T CID=2p RIC=1T CIC=3p CMRR=10k FCMRR=1k PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k
*   FPSRR=1k VCCN=5 VEEN=0 ENOISE=15n FCEN=1k INOISE=0.1f ICCQ=1m
*   VHD=0.05 VLD=0.05 ICMHI=-0.1 ICMLO=-0.1 VK=0.05 ROUT=100 ISRC=40m
*   ISNK=40m VXO=0 COUT=2p
*   (RIC=1T / RID=1T are fine; the Gmin of the simulator dominates.)
*   VCMN defaults to 2.5 V here (mid-supply).
*==============================================================================
